{"timestamp": "2026-03-13T06:12:55.268160Z", "step": "CHAT_OPENAI_API_RESPONSE", "message": "OpenAI API raw response (before raise_for_status)", "status_code": 200, "response_body": "{\n  \"id\": \"chatcmpl-DIq3NZEOUFKTz7aD6NG9lt8I3ROch\",\n  \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n  \"created\": 1773382369,\n  \"model\": \"gpt-4.1-mini-2025-04-14\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    {\n      \"index\": 0,\n      \"message\": {\n        \"role\": \"assistant\",\n        \"content\": \"Certainly! An ECG (electrocardiogram) records the electrical activity of the heart and displays it as a waveform with several key components. Here are the main components of an ECG and what they represent:\\n\\n1. **P wave**  \\n   - Represents atrial depolarization.  \\n   - This is when the electrical impulse spreads through the atria, causing them to contract and push blood into the ventricles.\\n\\n2. **PR interval**  \\n   - The time from the start of the P wave to the start of the QRS complex.  \\n   - Reflects the time the electrical impulse takes to travel from the atria through the AV node and into the ventricles.\\n\\n3. **QRS complex**  \\n   - Represents ventricular depolarization.  \\n   - This is when the ventricles contract to pump blood to the lungs and the rest of the body.  \\n   - It is usually a sharp, tall, and narrow waveform.\\n\\n4. **ST segment**  \\n   - The flat section between the end of the QRS complex and the start of the T wave.  \\n   - Represents the period when the ventricles are depolarized and beginning to repolarize.\\n\\n5. **T wave**  \\n   - Represents ventricular repolarization.  \\n   - This is when the ventricles recover electrically and prepare for the next contraction.\\n\\n6. **QT interval**  \\n   - The time from the start of the QRS complex to the end of the T wave.  \\n   - Reflects the total time for ventricular depolarization and repolarization.\\n\\nEach of these components helps clinicians assess heart rhythm, detect abnormalities, and diagnose various cardiac conditions. If you want, I can also explain how to interpret these components in different clinical scenarios.\",\n        \"refusal\": null,\n        \"annotations\": []\n      },\n      \"logprobs\": null,\n      \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"usage\": {\n    \"prompt_tokens\": 30,\n    \"completion_tokens\": 357,\n    \"total_tokens\": 387,\n    \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n      \"cached_tokens\": 0,\n      \"audio_tokens\": 0\n    },\n    \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n      \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\n      \"audio_tokens\": 0,\n      \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\n      \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\n    }\n  },\n  \"service_tier\": \"default\",\n  \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_5e793402c9\"\n}\n"}
